> keys content/sample factions.toml city_watch
factions.toml › city_watch can have:
  defectors: a table
    Does the faction joined take a member of its enemies? The last rule must have no conditions.
  deserters: a table
    Does each enemy faction someone is in let them go? The last rule must have no conditions.
  expel_standing_change: a number from -100.00 to 100.00, -20.00 by default
    The change in standing with the faction when it expels someone.
  exposed: a table
    On learning a member is secretly in a faction it's in conflict with: keep, demote or expel them? "Current" is the faction that found out, "target" the secret one. The last rule must have no conditions.
  leave_standing_change: a number from -100.00 to 100.00, 0.00 by default
    The change in standing with the faction when someone leaves of their own accord.
  secret_members: true or false, false by default
    Whether characters may belong to it secretly, unknown to anyone outside it. Needs knowledge.model witnessed or ripple (DESIGN.md §10.4).
> keys content/sample factions.toml city_watch.ranks
factions.toml › city_watch.ranks can have:
  an item at the end
> keys content/sample characters.toml
characters.toml can have:
  an entry by a new id
> assert keys content/sample factions.toml city_watch.alignment == factions.toml › city_watch.alignment has every key it can
> assert keys content/sample factions.toml nobody == error: nothing at nobody in factions.toml
